{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260615044337dd2df4a840d44df8","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have a comprehensive view of the implementation. Let me analyze what I've found:\n\n## Key Information from the Review:\n\n### Test Results\n- All tests pass: 144 passed, 20 test files\n- Build, typecheck, lint, boundaries all pass\n- Epic gate: `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all` passes\n\n### Implementation Status (from team-impl-log.md)\n- Stories 0-6: All implemented and verified accepted\n- Current state: EPIC_CLOSEOUT_BLOCKED_ON_PRODUCT_RULING\n- Latest epic review artifacts show 3 reviews (block, block, revise)\n- Epic fixes applied:\n  - Story 1 --resume now uses PI `ctx.ui.select` for interactive multiple-candidate selection\n  - Story 3 corpora now load recorded JSONL PI lifecycle fixtures\n  - EF-001 LHC retirement snapshot updated for current exported SDK names\n\n### Accepted Risks / Deviations\n1. **Local PI extension types** (src/pi/types.ts) - Acceptable because PI packages aren't build-time dependencies yet; strongly-typed mirror of verified v0.79.2\n2. **initLhc thin wrapper over createSdk** - Spec-anticipated by tech-arch A-4 / tech-design Q2\n3. **Story 1 SV-001 reload reconstruction** - Reload now re-resolves from the durable LHC registry; exact-prior-thread reconstruction deferred\n4. **Story 1 SV-002 --resume operator selection** - PI v0.79.2 has no interactive input/selection surface; picker implemented with ctx.ui.notify and auto-selects most-recent (NOW FIXED with ctx.ui.select per epic fix)\n5. **Story 2 SV-001 residual** - Identity-less + position-less + same-content event can collide - documented limitation (unreachable on real hook path)\n\n\n6. **Fork derived-form reuse** - v1 requeues derived forms rather than copying/reusing ready forms because provenance-identity safety is not implemented yet\n\nI see additional architectural nuances around fork behavior and interaction limits. The implementation now supports more sophisticated user selection mechanisms, with careful handling of thread resumption and identity management. The documented risks reflect a pragmatic approach to managing complex edge cases while maintaining core functionality.\n\nThe system demonstrates careful boundary management, ensuring robust extension loading and thread initialization processes. Key safeguards include:\n- Strict type checking with fail-closed stubs\n- Validated default model assignments\n- Comprehensive PI interaction models\n\nProduction path integrity is maintained through precise validation of extension hooks and inference configurations, with deliberate safeguards preventing unintended operations.\n\nThe testing strategy comprehensively covers critical scenarios:\n- Duplicate delivery protection mechanisms\n- Capture failure isolation protocols\n- Adapter boundary validation\n\nFork testing ensures thread integrity by verifying:\n- Source thread immutability\n- Accurate replay seeding\n- Proper derived form requeuing\n\nThe architecture risk assessment confirms the test suite's robust coverage of core system behaviors.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a08bfa87-d15f-49ef-98e9-3889acacbbb4","uuid":"62d6a096-535f-42e9-a57f-eea0eb635fbf"}
