\n2. Story 1 exact-prior-thread reload - re-resolves from registry (design constraint)\n\nI'll continue analyzing the production path and overall outcome. The exact-prior-thread reload using registry resolution represents a deliberate design approach to maintain thread consistency. This method ensures thread integrity across different execution contexts.\n\nThe production path demonstrates robust handling of thread management and type interactions, with careful consideration of architectural constraints and potential limitations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a08bfa87-d15f-49ef-98e9-3889acacbbb4","uuid":"83e21f3b-de6d-42a5-8033-99f565d97939"}
