{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260615044359c8f68e0535a84d02","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review of the epic artifacts, implementation codebase, and test results, here is my EpicVerifierProviderPayload:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"Cross-story consistency verified: plain-data-only rule enforced across all lifecycle paths (SessionState contains only ThreadRef + flags, no PI objects retained)\",\n    \"Thread resolution logic is consistent across launch modes (new, continue, resume, reload) - resolveReloadThread correctly re-resolves from durable registry\",\n    \"Capture flow is consistent: index.ts orchestrates map → accumulate → batch flush through converter for all message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select hooks\",\n    \"Fork detection and seeding logic properly wired in session_start handler - both hook-based and session-tree fallback evidence paths implemented\",\n    \"Startup validation correctly runs after instance creation but before capture begins, leaving capture running on validation failure (AC-5.3)\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"Module boundaries respected: check-boundaries.mjs passes (20 src files checked)\",\n    \"Interfaces match tech design Interface Definitions - all required exports present with correct signatures\",\n    \"Hook rail matches EPIC_1_HOOKS specification - all observe-only hooks registered, context hook correctly omitted\",\n    \"Two documented deviations are appropriate given environmental constraints: (1) local PI types in src/pi/types.ts mirror verified v0.79.2 contract since @earendil-works/* packages aren't build dependencies yet; (2) initLhc is thin wrapper over createSdk per tech-arch A-4\",\n    \"Architecture-risk tests from tech design are all implemented: restart/reattach, idempotency/dedup, adapter-boundary classification, atomicity/isolation, source-vs-der