ctivate path (orig SV-001): fixed (real activate/hook lifecycle wired).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:122:  - HARDENING NOTE (Story 2): if a future PI version (or a non-PI host) can deliver capture events with NO stable entry id AND NO source position, the id-less idempotency fallback cannot distinguish a re-delivered event from a distinct same-content one across a fresh attach. Mitigation if ever needed: require the host to stamp a durable per-event id/position at intake, or persist the connector sourceSeq high-water mark across attaches. Not reachable with PI v0.79.2 (every session entry carries id+parentId).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:134:  - SV-04-005: fixed by direct bounded impl-lead edit; fallback detection now reads previousSessionFile and current session entries, then uses shared ids / parentId links as PI session-tree evidence.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:136:  - Derived form reuse deviation: accepted-risk — v1 requeues derived forms rather than copying/reusing ready forms because provenance-identity safety is not implemented yet. This preserves correctness and was approved in artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/story-lead/001-ruling-response-001.json.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:149:  - Production createModelCall now routes through PI/pi-ai when available, classifies host/provider failures, and keeps deterministic seams for tests.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:162:  - Default assignments now use production-reachable PI lane `openai-codex/gpt-5.4`; startup validation reports unreachable lanes visibly while capture continues.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:182:- Epic Review Status: re-review pending after fixing Story 1 interactive `--resume` with `ctx.ui.select`.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:185:  - Story 3 corpora now load recorded JSONL PI lifecycle fixtures from packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora instead of synthetic stand-ins.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:187:- Epic Reverify Status: re-review pending.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:192:- M0 inputs pending per spec: recorded corpora are Story 3 fixtures; image/file-ref handling (safe interim = degrade-to-runtime_note) and tool-call rendering are M0 decisions. Story 3 fixture breadth widens as corpora arrive.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:193:- createSdk→initLhc rename (A-4) pending but mechanical; spec uses initLhc.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:201:- Tech-design shape: two-file (tech-design.md + test-plan.md). Prompt inserts: both absent. Epic 1 is observe-only.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:7:This plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:53:| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:61:| TC-2.2 | One-prompt-two-tools-then-answer → exactly one LHC turn, `turn_end` at agent_end | the Flow 2 worked-example corpus | exactly one `turn_end`; emitted at `agent_end`; per-step PI `turn_end`s produce none |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:84:| TC-3.1 *(risk: source-vs-derived)* | Fork creates new thread; source receives no writes | capture a thread, fork it | new thread created; source **logical read-back** (events/messages/turns) unchanged; fork point resolved from `session_before_fork` hook (PI session tree as Epic-1 fallback) |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:92:| TC-4.1 | Function resolves (provider,model) via registry, returns text | fake registry + complete returning text | returns `{ok:true,text}` for a single-turn message list |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:93:| TC-4.2 | Two kinds → different (provider,model) both route in one session | two assignments, two fakes | each call routes by its keys; both succeed |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:101:| TC-4.5 | Captured thread's queued derivation invokes fn + persists outcome | captured thread; fakes (one text, one failure); `drainSettled` | at least one ready derived form + one classified failure, both queryable via inspect/health |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:118:| TC-5.6 | Incomplete/unknown assignment fails loud at init | missing kind / unknown prompt / placeholder | construction throws actionable error; no placeholder masks it |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:138:Each chunk: write skeletons (structured-result stubs for services/adapters/handlers; `NotImplementedError` for pure algorithms) → Red (tests written, failing for the right reason — never asserting on `NotImplementedError`) → Green (implement to pass). Exit each chunk on `green-verify`.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:142:- **Skeleton:** all interface exports (`tech-design.md` → Interface Definitions); `index.ts` hook registration with stubbed handlers; `state.ts` complete (plain data, no stub).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:143:- **Red:** fixture-invariant tests (corpus shapes, synthetic coherence, temp-thread create+reopen); extension-loads smoke; package verification scripts/config present.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:149:- **Skeleton:** `instance.ts`, `thread-resolution.ts`, `picker.ts` as structured-result stubs.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:156:- **Skeleton:** `map-message.ts`, `turn-accumulator.ts`, `idempotency.ts` (`NotImplementedError`); `converter.ts` (structured result).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:157:- **Red:** TC-2.1–2.9 + idempotency + atomicity risk tests, failing. Turn-derivation goldens (worked example, abort, hard-kill) written here.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:166:- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass. Consumes M0 corpora; widens as they arrive.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:172:- **Green:** fork-point detection (`session_before_fork` hook; PI session tree as Epic-1 fallback), replay-seed, requeue, source read-only.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:199:| Manual: load into real PI, run a session, inspect | manual | the wide pass; not automated, recorded in tech-design Testing Strategy |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:201:No suite is skipped on auth availability — the closed-loop test (TC-4.5) uses a deterministic `ModelCall` fake, not a live provider, so it always runs.\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:38:  // call id — never a block scan (anti-shim requirement).\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:45:    state        TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (state IN ('pending','ready','failed','blocked')),\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:69:  // F-02 backfill: pending form rows for work queued before v5 existed, so\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:72:    SELECT 'message', json_extract(source_ref, '$.messageId'), 'smoothed_prompt', 'pending', 1\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:75:    SELECT 'message', json_extract(source_ref, '$.messageId'), 'tool_result_summary', 'pending', 1\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:78:    SELECT 'turn', json_extract(source_ref, '$.turnId'), 'turn_rendering', 'pending', 1\npackages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:81:    SELECT 'turn', json_extract(source_ref, '$.turnId'), 'lower_band_projection', 'pending', 1\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:117:// The one way work is scheduled (DD-5): the work row, the form's `pending`\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:121:// resets an existing row to pending at the enqueued source version.\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:127:     VALUES (?, ?, ?, 'pending', ?)\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:129:       state = 'pending', content = NULL, reason = NULL, metadata = NULL,\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:185:// v5, shared/storage.ts): the backfill created pending derived_form rows at\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:188:// form as pending forever, breaking AC-1.9/DD-1 for upgraded threads.\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:286:// upsert — the pending row exists from enqueue; a write that finds no row at\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:447:// commit together (anti-shim: a check-then-enqueue split across transactions\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts:1:// Local declarations of the pi-ai completion surface the connector consumes.\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts:3:// These mirror `@earendil-works/pi-ai` as verified by the wiring research\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts:4:// (docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md). The pi-ai package\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts:5:// is not yet a build dependency of this workspace, so the connector declares the\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts:7:// dependency lands (Spec Deviation, recorded in the story payload).\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts:11:/** Completion context passed to pi-ai's complete() function. */\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts:16:/** The pi-ai complete() signature. */\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts:21:/** Error shapes pi-ai's complete() may throw or return. */\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts:28:/** Known pi-ai error codes/types that map to LHC failure kinds. */\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:27:} from \"../fixtures/synthetic.js\";\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:155:describe(\"Story 2: converter — connector fallback idempotency\", () => {\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:214:      counts: { ready: 0, pending: 0, retrying: 0, failed: 1, blocked: 0 },\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:3:**Status:** Draft for review. **Ready for tech design once M0 lands.** Per the PRD's M0 gate, this epic's capture-verification tests consume the M0 corpus fixtures (Story 3) and two M0 decisions must be settled before tech design: the image/file-reference handling choice and the tool-call rendering choice (A5). These are named as M0 inputs below, not left as open tech design questions.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:17:**The LHC thread is the system of record for the conversation, and the registry is the catalog of threads.** What an earlier draft got wrong was treating PI's session file as the place a thread mapping had to be stored and recovered; it does not, because a thread's identity arrives at launch — the operator selects it — so there is no mapping to recover and no pointer to keep in sync. What is true *in this epic* is narrower than \"PI has no session file\": this epic is observe-only, so **PI still runs its own session normally** — it persists its session, serves its own context to the model, and tracks its own fork lineage, exactly as vanilla PI does. LHC records alongside that as the durable conversation record. PI's session file becomes vestigial only in Feature 2, when LHC's served context replaces PI's transcript; until then the two coexist, and nothing the model sees changes.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:22:- A **derivation** produces a **derived form** from recorded content (for example, a summary of a tool result). The seven derived-form kinds are `smoothed_prompt`, `tool_call_summary`, `tool_result_summary`, `turn_rendering`, `lower_band_projection`, `chunk_summary_detailed`, `chunk_summary_brief`. Each derivation runs through one **model-call function** the host supplies.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:27:**M0** is the pre-epic period that produces the recorded PI **corpora** (real sessions captured to fixtures) and the **converter** prototype (PI events → intake events). Live recon (June 2026) already established the PI event shapes this epic depends on; M0's remaining work is corpus breadth, the productionized converter, and derivation dial-in. This epic's capture-verification tests consume M0 corpora as fixtures.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:53:**Key Constraint:** This epic is observe-only. The extension must add no perceptible latency and must change nothing the model sees — PI's native context handling stays in control. A capture failure must never break the PI session: writable-thread failures become durable, queryable gaps; store-unavailable failures become visible extension diagnostics because the gap cannot be written.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:79:- Derivation prompt and model dial-in (quality tuning) — the paired M0 dial-in period; this epic ships default assignments and proves the routing, not the tuning.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:92:| A-2 | M0 delivers recorded PI corpora as test fixtures and a converter prototype to productionize. | Pending (M0) | The epic spec stands, but the build and the verification flow's tests wait on M0 corpora. Capture ACs are spec-complete; their fixtures are an M0 input. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:97:| A-7 | The image / file-reference handling decision (placeholder vs. extending the intake payload schema) is settled by M0 before this epic's tech design. | Pending (M0 gate) | The converter's content-part mapping (Flow 2) depends on it. Recon found `@file.png` stays literal text in print mode; the interactive paste shape is uncaptured. M0 corpora establish frequency; the decision is an M0 output, not a tech design question. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:98:| A-8 | The LHC registry gains a `cwd` column (set at thread creation), a `--resume` cwd filter on `listThreads`, partial-id match on `resolve`, and a `title` set at creation / updated on rename. | **Epic 1 implementation scope** (LHC-side); not yet in LHC code | AC-1.6 and AC-1.7 depend on these directly, so they are a build prerequisite for Story 1, not optional polish. The work is small and mechanical — the registry already carries id/title/created — but \"small\" is not \"non-blocking\": the cwd-scoped picker and partial-id resolve cannot pass without them. They are gated before Story 1's launch-mode ACs. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:223:**AC-5.5:** A user override — a different provider, model, or prompt for any kind — takes effect on the next session start with no code change. An incomplete or unknown assignment fails loudly at initialization with an actionable error, never a silent skip or a placeholder default that masks the misconfiguration.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:254:| `session_before_fork` | `entryId`, `position` | The fork point when present; otherwise PI's session tree is Epic-1 fallback evidence (permanent lineage is LHC metadata, Feature 2+) |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:281:Image and file-reference content parts: LHC intake payloads are text today. Handling (placeholder vs. payload-schema extension) is an M0 decision (A-7), not a tech design question; until that decision lands, the converter must not silently drop a content part without recording the omission.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:298:**Worked example.** A user asks one question that triggers two tool calls, then gets a final answer. PI emits:\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:376:`FormKind` is the seven derivation kinds: `smoothed_prompt`, `tool_call_summary`, `tool_result_summary`, `turn_rendering`, `lower_band_projection`, `chunk_summary_detailed`, `chunk_summary_brief`. `prompt` must name a registered prompt. Initialization fails loudly if any kind is missing, references an unknown prompt, or carries a placeholder.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:391:- **Fail loud on misconfiguration.** Missing, unknown, or placeholder assignments fail at initialization with an actionable error, not a silent skip.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:399:3. **Converter structure** — the converter is the productionized M0 prototype; how it consumes `message_end` streams and emits batched `MessageEventInput[]` per the `intakeStream.messageEvents` contract.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:402:> Thread mapping is **not** a tech design question — the thread is resolved at launch through the registry (Flow 1), with no stored PI-session→thread mapping, so the former \"mapping persistence shape\" and \"resolution by external key\" questions are dissolved, not deferred. (PI keeps its own session file in this observe-only epic; it is just not where thread identity lives.)\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:404:> Image / file-reference handling is **not** a tech design question — it is an M0 decision (A-7), settled before this epic's tech design per the PRD's M0 gate.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:414:**Delivers:** The walking skeleton: extension package scaffold, the PI extension entry point and hook registration rail, the plain-data-only state holder, the LHC instance init/dispose seam (stubbed), test fixture and corpus-loading harness, and typed fail-closed stubs.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:417:**Boundary / risk notes:** Stubs fail closed, never fake success (tech arch convention). The plain-data-only rule (AC-1.3) is established here as the state-holder shape so no later story is tempted to cache a context object.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:443:**Prerequisite:** Story 2. Consumes M0 corpora as fixtures.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:444:**Boundary / risk notes:** This story's fixtures are the M0 corpora (A-2). If corpora are not yet broad, the story builds the replay-equality and inspect machinery against whatever corpora exist and widens as M0 delivers.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:538:- **TC-2.2** — A one-prompt-two-tools-then-answer corpus (the worked example) yields exactly one LHC turn with one `turn_end` at agent-run completion; PI's per-step `turn_end`s produce none.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:546:- **TC-3.1** — Fork creates a new thread; the source thread receives no writes — its logical read-back (events, messages, turns) is unchanged. Detection resolves the fork point from the `session_before_fork` hook, with PI's session tree as available fallback evidence in Epic 1, not from a fork reason code.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:559:- **TC-5.6** — An incomplete or unknown assignment fails loudly at initialization with an actionable error; no placeholder default masks it.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:573:- [x] Assumptions carry status and impact-if-wrong, including the M0 dependency\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:574:- [x] Data contracts cover every operation the flows exercise, including the turn-derivation worked example, abort/crash shapes, and error shapes\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:575:- [x] The load-bearing turn-derivation contract (PI turn ≠ LHC turn) is stated with a worked example\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:579:- [ ] Consumer test: a tech designer can design from this without asking foundational questions — pending review\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts:23:      // a real recorded sequence, not an empty stub, and a closed turn\npackages/pi-lhc/test/inference/mode