{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/004-epic-review.json'","aggregated_output":"{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Two reviewers reached different outcomes (revise vs. block) primarily over whether documented accepted-risk deviations should block epic closeout. Reviewer-1 (claude-code) treated Story 1's accepted-risk deviations (reload using cwd-most-recent, --resume failing closed for multiple candidates) as resolved via impl-lead ruling, surfacing only EF-001 as non-blocking. Reviewer-2 (codex) correctly identified that these are material departures from the literal AC contract (EV-002, EV-003) and that corpus fixtures are synthetic stand-ins rather than recorded PI corpora (EV-001). All three findings are supported by code evidence: index.ts lines 192-200 (defaultSelectThread returns null for multiple candidates), thread-resolution.ts lines 141-147 (reload uses cwd-most-recent), and replay.ts lines 36-38 (synthetic stand-in data). The team implementation log records these as approved accepted-risk deviations due to PI v0.79.2 API constraints and M0 dependency status. Both reviewers agreed gates pass (142 tests, 20 files). The canonical review confirms all three findings remain supported but recommends non-blocking given documented approvals and upstream requests.\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 0-4 are complete with verified receipts in team-impl-log.md\",\"Stories 5-6 (Inference Host Routing + Startup Validation) implemented and gated\",\"Cross-story consistency maintained: plain-data-only state, converter architecture, and idempotency design align across stories\",\"Capture spine (S0→S1→S2→S3) is strictly linear as designed\",\"Fork (S4) and Inference (S5) branch correctly from the capture spine and lifecycle foundation\",\"All configured gates pass: pi-lhc verify-all = 142 tests passing across 20 test files\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Turn-derivation contract (PI turn ≠ LHC turn) correctly implemented: TurnAccumulator ignores PI's per-step turn_end and emits exactly one LHC turn_end at agent_end\",\"Converter follows tech design: map-message (pure) → turn-accumulator (stateful) → converter (orchestrates batch flush)\",\"Idempotency uses 4-tier precedence system (entryId → toolCallId → responseId → fingerprint) as specified\",\"Fork detection uses both hook-based (session_before_fork) and session-tree fallback as Epic 1 design allows\",\"Plain-data-only rule enforced: SessionState holds only threadRef and flags; no PI objects retained\",\"Architecture-risk tests present: restart/reload, idempotency double-replay, adapter-boundary failure classification, atomicity isolation, source-vs-derived fork immutability\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 6 AC-sets (AC-1.1 through AC-6.3) have corresponding tests\",\"Test coverage: 142 tests across 20 test files pass (pi-lhc verify-all)\",\"Corpus replay tests consume synthetic fixtures pending M0 delivery; replay harness machinery is complete\",\"Closed-loop test (TC-4.5) proves capture→derivation→recorded-outcome end-to-end through real scheduler + drainSettled\",\"Architecture-risk tests cover: restart survival, idempotency dedup, adapter-boundary classification, atomicity isolation, source-vs-derived fork immutability\",\"TC-6.1 (corpus replay) and TC-6.2 (deterministic re-replay) provide golden-case coverage against synthetic fixtures\",\"Coverage gaps acknowledged: M0 corpus breadth pending; image/file-ref handling decision deferred (degrade-to-runtime_note interim in place)\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"pi-ai boundary is real: createModelCall dynamically imports @earendil-works/pi-ai at runtime (model-call.ts lines 78-90), returning classified failure when unavailable—never fabricated text\",\"Default assignments use real PI model (openai-codex/gpt-5.4 per PI v0.79.2 catalog), not placeholder\",\"Test fixtures use deterministic ModelCall fakes (fakeModelCallText, fakeModelCallFailure, fakeModelCallRouter) at mock boundary as designed\",\"Closed-loop test wires through real scheduler + drainSettled, not fake derivation path\",\"Replay harness drives through real converter + intakeStream into temp SQLite threads, not mocked intake\",\"Local PI type declarations (src/pi/types.ts, src/inference/pi-ai.ts) are documented deviation—verified mirror of v0.79.2 research, environmental necessity\",\"initLhc wrapper over createSdk is spec-anticipated mechanical rename (tech-design A-4/Q2)\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EC-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production --resume does not resolve operator selection for multiple cwd threads\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md AC-1.7 requires --resume to list cwd threads and resolve operator's selection. packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:192-200 (defaultSelectThread) presents candidates via ctx.ui.notify but returns null for multiple candidates, directing operator to relaunch with --session. Test TC-1.7 (thread-resolution.test.ts:255-293) asserts this fail-closed behavior. Team impl-log records as accepted-risk due to PI v0.79.2 lacking interactive input/selection API; upstream request filed.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\",\"TC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EC-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Reload can attach wrong thread because it uses cwd-most-recent instead of resolved threadId\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md AC-1.5 requires reload to reconstruct from durable state (resolved thread id). packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:141-147 (resolveReloadThread) returns cwd-most-recent for no-flag and --resume reloads. Test TC-1.5 (thread-resolution.test.ts:336-373) proves correct only when no newer cwd thread exists. Team impl-log records as accepted-risk; design forbids PI-session→thread mapping and PI lacks extension API for exact thread recovery.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.5\",\"TC-1.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EF-001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"LHC verify fails due to FORM_KINDS not in SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS list\",\"evidence\":\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:33 exports FORM_KINDS, but packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts:20-49 (SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS) does not include it. WORK_KIND_REGISTRY is correctly listed at line 27. This causes retirement.test.ts:62 to fail when checking export list equality.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"LHC-Epic-05-TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EF-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Capture verification uses synthetic corpus fixtures pending M0 delivery\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md AC-6.1 requires replaying recorded PI corpora. packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/*.jsonl contain handcrafted AgentMessage data. packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:36-38 comment states 'synthetic PI source messages (the stand-in until M0 delivers recordings)'. Team impl-log records Story 3 accepted with M0 inputs pending; fixture breadth will widen as corpora arrive.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/*.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\",\"A-2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EF-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Local PI type declarations remain pending package installation\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts and packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts declare local types instead of importing from @earendil-works packages (not yet installed in workspace). Team impl-log records as accepted-risk with documented plan to swap to real imports when @earendil-works packages installed (Epic 2/4 packaging).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"Story-0-deviation-1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EF-004\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"initLhc→createSdk rename pending in LHC package\",\"evidence\":\"initLhc is thin wrapper over createSdk. Tech-design A-4/Q2 notes this as spec-anticipated mechanical rename. Team impl-log records as pending mechanical change.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"A-4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Human ruling or spec update for production --resume behavior under PI v0.79.2 when multiple cwd threads exist (EC-001)\",\"Human ruling or design update for exact reload thread identity without PI-thread mapping record (EC-002)\",\"Replace handcrafted corpus jsonl files with real recorded PI corpora or formally narrow AC-6.1 before epic closeout (EF-002)\",\"Add FORM_KINDS to SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS in retirement.test.ts (EF-001)\",\"createSdk→initLhc rename in LHC package (mechanical, A-4)\",\"Local PI type declarations swap to real imports when @earendil-works packages installed (Epic 2/4)\",\"PI extension input/selection API for real --resume picker and exact-thread reload (upstream request filed)\",\"M0 decision A-7: image/file-reference handling (placeholder vs intake-schema extension); degrade-to-runtime_note interim in place\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"eb4b0d27-4fdc-4cd2-bdeb-0670bd09533b\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 0-4 are complete and verified with clear receipts in team-impl-log.md\",\"Stories 5-6 (Inference Host Routing + Startup Validation) are implemented and gated\",\"Cross-story consistency maintained: plain-data-only state, converter architecture, and idempotency design align across all stories\",\"The capture spine (S0→S1→S2→S3) is strictly linear as designed\",\"Fork (S4) and Inference (S5) branch correctly from the capture spine and lifecycle foundation\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The turn-derivation contract (PI turn ≠ LHC turn) is correctly implemented: TurnAccumulator ignores PI's per-step turn_end and emits exactly one LHC turn_end at agent_end\",\"The converter follows the tech design: map-message (pure) → turn-accumulator (stateful) → converter (orchestrates batch flush)\",\"Idempotency uses the 4-tier precedence system (entryId → toolCallId → responseId → fingerprint) as specified\",\"Fork detection uses both hook-based (session_before_fork) and session-tree fallback as Epic 1 design allows\",\"The plain-data-only rule is enforced: SessionState holds only threadRef and flags; no PI objects retained\",\"The architecture-risk tests from tech-design §Testing Strategy are present: restart/reload, idempotency double-replay, adapter-boundary failure classification, atomicity isolation, source-vs-derived fork immutability\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 6 AC-sets (AC-1.1 through AC-6.3) have corresponding tests\",\"Test coverage: 142 tests across 20 test files pass (pi-lhc verify-all)\",\"Corpus replay tests (Story 3) consume M0 corpora as fixtures and assert on read-back through real SQLite threads\",\"The closed-loop test (TC-4.5) proves capture→derivation→recorded-outcome end-to-end\",\"Architecture-risk tests cover: restart survival, idempotency dedup, adapter-boundary classification, atomicity isolation, source-vs-derived fork immutability, fixture validity, concurrency stale-write protection\",\"TC-6.1 (corpus replay) and TC-6.2 (deterministic re-replay) provide golden-case coverage\",\"Coverage gaps: limited M0 corpus breadth (widens as corpora arrive), image/file-ref handling decision pending (degrade-to-runtime_note interim is in place)\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The pi-ai boundary is real: createModelCall dynamically imports @earendil-works/pi-ai at runtime (model-call.ts line 78-90), returning classified failure when unavailable—never fabricated text\",\"Default assignments use a real PI model (openai-codex/gpt-5.4 per PI v0.79.2 catalog), not a placeholder\",\"Test fixtures use deterministic ModelCall fakes (fakeModelCallText, fakeModelCallFailure, fakeModelCallRouter) at the mock boundary as designed\",\"The closed-loop test wires through the real scheduler + drainSettled, not a fake derivation path\",\"The replay harness drives through the real converter + intakeStream into temp SQLite threads, not mocked intake\",\"Local PI type declarations (src/pi/types.ts, src/inference/pi-ai.ts) are a documented deviation—verified mirror of v0.79.2 research, environmental necessity, not a design change\",\"The initLhc wrapper over createSdk is a spec-anticipated mechanical rename (tech-design A-4/Q2)\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EF-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"LHC verify fails due to outdated SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS list\",\"evidence\":\"packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts:62 expects export list to match checked-in SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS, but actual exports include FORM_KINDS, WORK_KIND_REGISTRY, lookupWorkHandler, assembleWorkHandlerMap not in the list\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"LHC-Epic-05-TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":false}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EF-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"M0 inputs pending per spec\",\"evidence\":\"M0 corpora breadth for Story 3 fixtures; image/file-ref handling decision (A-7); tool-call rendering choice\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"A-2\",\"A-7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EF-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Local PI type declarations remain\",\"evidence\":\"src/pi/types.ts and src/inference/pi-ai.ts declare local types instead of importing from @earendil-works packages (not yet installed)\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"Story-0-deviation-1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EF-004\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"createSdk→initLhc rename pending\",\"evidence\":\"initLhc is a thin wrapper over createSdk; the mechanical rename is anticipated by tech-design A-4 but not yet landed in LHC\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"A-4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"M0 corpora: fixture breadth for Story 3 verification widens as corpora arrive\",\"M0 decision A-7: image/file-reference handling (placeholder vs intake-schema extension); degrade-to-runtime_note interim is in place\",\"createSdk→initLhc rename in LHC package (mechanical, A-4)\",\"Local PI type declarations swap to real imports when @earendil-works packages are installed (Epic 2/4 packaging)\",\"PI extension input/selection API: real --resume operator selection deferred until PI exposes the surface (upstream request filed)\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"ceb66fbc-9d9e-49df-84b3-7bd7b4702414\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 2, 4, 5, and 6 are broadly coherent: capture, turn derivation, fork replay, inference routing, and startup validation are wired through connector entry points and real LHC surfaces.\",\"Story 1 still has accepted-risk behavior that does not satisfy the literal epic contract: reload reattaches by cwd-most-recent for no-flag/resume launches, and production --resume cannot resolve an operator selection when more than one cwd thread exists.\",\"Story 3 does not meet the epic-level verification contract because the corpus fixtures are small handcrafted AgentMessage jsonl files, not recorded PI corpora with the real hook/lifecycle surface the epic requires.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The observe-only boundary is preserved: packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts registers no context hook, and capture does not alter what PI sends to the model.\",\"The converter module shape matches the tech design: map-message is pure, turn-accumulator owns LHC turn close, and converter writes through intakeStream.messageEvents.\",\"Reload behavior drifts from AC-1.5 and tech-design.md: the design says reload reconstructs from durable state, specifically the resolved thread id, while packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts falls back to cwd-most-recent for no-flag and --resume reloads.\",\"The --resume production path has a picker abstraction, but the default selector only notifies and returns null for multiple candidates, so the production path does not resolve the operator's selection required by AC-1.7.\",\"A recorded-risk note exists in docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md, but the epic and tech design were not updated to narrow AC-1.5, AC-1.7, or AC-6.1.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Flow 1 is incomplete against the written contract: new/continue/session resolution exists, but reload exact-thread reconstruction and production resume selection are not fully implemented.\",\"Flow 2 is covered by source and tests: ordered message mapping, turn derivation, runtime notes, idempotency, capture gaps, parallel tools, errors, and aborts are implemented.\",\"Flow 3 is implemented with replay seeding and derived-form requeue; source thread immutability is covered.\",\"Flow 4 is implemented through createModelCall over PI modelRegistry plus pi-ai dynamic import, with failure classification and closed-loop persisted outcomes covered by tests using injected completion/model-call boundaries.\",\"Flow 5 is implemented: assignments load defaults/overrides, startup validation reports unreachable lanes, and capture continues.\",\"Flow 6 is incomplete: replay is deterministic and compares durable read-back, but it does not consume real recorded PI corpora as required by AC-6.1.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapter was found in src capture/fork/inspect paths: capture uses real LHC intakeStream, fork replay uses intakeStream.messageEvents, and inspect reads real LHC surfaces.\",\"Test-only model-call fakes are confined to packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures and are not production code.\",\"createModelCall does not fabricate output when pi-ai is unavailable; it returns a classified failure.\",\"Material non-real verification path: packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/*.jsonl are handcrafted AgentMessage rows, and packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:36-38 still describes the corpus source as synthetic stand-in data.\",\"Material production limitation: packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:192-200 defaultSelectThread presents candidates through notify but resolves only a single candidate; multiple candidates return null instead of a selected thread.\",\"Material reload limitation: packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:141-147 resolves reload by cwd-most-recent, which is not durable resolved-thread-id reconstruction.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Capture verification does not use recorded PI corpora\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md:229-231 requires recorded PI corpus replay, including chatty/tool-heavy/parallel-tool/error-result/aborted-turn corpora. packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/*.jsonl contain handcrafted AgentMessage rows with no PI hook metadata or lifecycle events, and packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:36-38 still calls the source synthetic stand-in data.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/chatty.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/tool-heavy.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/parallel-tool.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/error-result.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/aborted-turn.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production --resume does not resolve operator selection for multiple cwd threads\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md:141 requires --resume to list cwd threads and resolve the operator's selection. packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:192-200 notifies the candidate list but returns a thread only when there is exactly one candidate; packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:255-292 asserts this fail-closed production behavior instead of a selected thread.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\",\"TC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Reload can attach the wrong thread because it uses cwd-most-recent instead of the resolved threadId\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md:137 requires reload to reconstruct from durable state, the resolved thread id, and continue on the same thread. packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:141-147 lists cwd threads and returns the last row for no-flag/--resume reloads. This only proves correct when no newer cwd thread exists, which is the narrow scenario covered by packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:336-373.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.5\",\"TC-1.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"NF-001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Configured gates pass\",\"evidence\":\"Ran pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify and pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all; both completed successfully with 20 test files and 142 tests passing.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Local PI and pi-ai type declarations remain a runtime packaging boundary\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts declares the consumed PI API slice and packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts declares the pi-ai completion type because the real PI packages are not workspace dependencies; packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts dynamically imports @earendil-works/pi-ai at runtime.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Derived-form reuse remains deferred while fork correctness is preserved\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts seeds forked threads by replay and does not copy ready derived forms; AC-3.3 permits requeue when reuse safety cannot be proven.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Replace handcrafted corpus jsonl files with real recorded PI corpora or formally narrow AC-6.1 before passing the epic.\",\"Human ruling or spec update needed for production --resume behavior under PI v0.79.2 when multiple cwd threads exist.\",\"Human ruling or design update needed for exact reload thread identity without a PI-thread mapping record.\",\"If the accepted-risk lifecycle behavior stands, update epic.md and tech-design.md so AC-1.5 and AC-1.7 match the implementation and tests.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/004-epic-review.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:53:15.457Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:56:55.175Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
