{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260615044706942a890746cf4f1f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"block\",\n  \"reviewerLabels\": [\n    \"epic-reviewer-1\",\n    \"epic-reviewer-2\"\n  ],\n  \"reconciliationSummary\": \"Two independent reviewers produced conflicting outcomes (pass vs block). The reverifier's task is to determine whether the blocking findings (EV-001, EV-002) are substantiated by the codebase and epic artifacts, and whether the non-blocking design risks cited by Reviewer 1 (NF-002, NF-004) properly account for the issues raised by Reviewer 2. Per conservative reverify protocol, blockers are downgraded only when explicit evidence disproves them. The reverification examined the disputed surfaces: (1) Story 3's corpus verification path against AC-6.1's recorded PI corpora requirement; (2) Story 1's reload semantics against AC-1.5's exact-thread reconstruction requirement. Findings follow.\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"Stories 2-5 are coherent across the capture/fork/inference/startup-validation spine: all paths route through connector entry points and real LHC intake/scheduler/inspect surfaces (both reviewers agree).\",\n    \"Story 1 has a lifecycle coverage gap: reload for no-flag and --resume launches reattaches by cwd-most-recent registry row, not by durable resolved-threadId reconstruction (Reviewer 2 block EV-002; Reviewer 1 NF-002 as accepted constraint).\",\n    \"Story 3 does not satisfy the epic-level verification contract: corpus fixtures are simplified AgentMessage JSONL rows paired with handcrafted expected events, not recorded PI hook/lifecycle corpora as required by AC-6.1 (Reviewer 2 block EV-001; Reviewer 1 claims real corpora used).\",\n    \"Plain-data-only rule is enforced across all lifecycle paths—SessionState contains only ThreadRef + flags, no PI objects retained (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Capture flow is consistent: index.ts orchestrates map → accumulate → batch flush through converter for all message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select hooks (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Fork detection and seeding logic properly wired in session_start handler with both hook-based and session-tree fallback evidence paths (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Startup validation correctly runs after instance creation but before capture begins, leaving capture running on validation failure per AC-5.3 (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"The --resume picker has an interactive ctx.ui.select path for multi-candidate scenarios, while headless multi-candidate resume remains fail-closed requiring explicit --session (Reviewer 2; not disputed).\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"Module boundaries respected: check-boundaries.mjs passes (20 src files checked) (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Interfaces match tech design Interface Definitions—all required exports present with correct signatures (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Hook rail matches EPIC_1_HOOKS specification—all observe-only hooks registered, context hook correctly omitted (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Converter architecture matches tech design: map-message is pure, TurnAccumulator owns the LHC turn boundary, converter flushes through intakeStream.messageEvents (both reviewers agree).\",\n    \"Local PI types in src/pi/types.ts mirror verified v0.79.2 contract since @earendil-works/* packages aren't build dependencies yet (Reviewer 1 NF-004; Reviewer 2 NF-002).\",\n    \"initLhc is thin wrapper over createSdk per tech-arch A-4—mechanical rename pending LHC package change (Reviewer 1 NF-005).\",\n    \"The observe-only boundary is preserved: index.ts registers no context hook, capture does not alter PI's model context path (Reviewer 2; not disputed).\",\n    \"Derived-form reuse is deferred while fork correctness is preserved—fork requeues derived forms on new thread rather than copying/reusing per tech design I-2 (Reviewer 1 NF-003; Reviewer 2 NF-003).\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"All 33 TCs mapped to tests—test-plan.md TC→Test mapping fully realized (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Architecture-risk tests present: 7 tests covering restart survival, idempotency double-replay, failure classification, capture isolation, fork source immutability, fixture validity, concurrency (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Foundation tests present: 7 tests covering corpus shapes, synthetic builders, temp-thread factory, extension-load smoke, verification-config (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Total test coverage: 144 tests passing across 20 test files (Reviewer 1; Reviewer 2 gates also passed).\",\n    \"Flows 2-5 are covered by source and tests: ordered capture, turn derivation, idempotency, fork replay, model-call routing, classified failures, startup validation (Reviewer 2).\",\n    \"Flow 1 is partially covered: launch creation, named resolution, continue, interactive resume, shutdown implemented; exact same-thread reload not implemented for no-flag and --resume launches (Reviewer 2).\",\n    \"Flow 6 is incomplete against AC-6.1: replay is deterministic and compares events/messages/turns, but does not consume recorded PI corpora as required (Reviewer 2 EV-001).\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"Production createModelCall uses real PI modelRegistry.find and hasConfiguredAuth—no fake adapters in production inference path (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Extension entry point (index.ts activate) registers real hooks with production defaults (~/.lhc registry, process.argv launch flags, real ModelCall) (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"No shims or placeholders in production capture path—converter, idempotency, turn-accumulator all use real implementations (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Startup validation uses real PI modelRegistry for reachability probes—correctly classifies unknown_model vs auth_not_configured (Reviewer 1; not disputed).\",\n    \"Test-only model-call fakes are confined to packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures and are not production code (Reviewer 2; not disputed).\",\n    \"Material non-real verification path: packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/*.jsonl are simplified AgentMessage rows with no PI hook metadata or lifecycle events, and packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts hand-builds expected events instead of replaying recorded PI hook/lifecycle corpora (Reviewer 2 EV-001; disputed with Reviewer 1's 'real recorded JSONL PI lifecycle data' claim).\",\n    \"createModelCall does not fabricate completion text when @earendil-works/pi-ai is unavailable—returns a classified failure (Reviewer 2; not disputed).\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"EV-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"title\": \"Capture verification does not use recorded PI corpora\",\n      \"evidence\": \"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:229-231 requires recorded PI corpus replay, including chatty/tool-heavy/parallel-tool/error-result/aborted-turn corpora. packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/chatty.jsonl and tool-heavy.jsonl contain plain AgentMessage rows with no PI hook metadata or lifecycle events. packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:27-38 hand-builds the expected LHC events for chatty. This fails to satisfy AC-6.1's requirement for recorded PI hook/lifecycle corpora. Reviewer 1's claim that 'real recorded JSONL PI lifecycle data' is used conflicts with the actual fixture structure.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/chatty.jsonl\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/tool-heavy.jsonl\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/parallel-tool.jsonl\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/error-result.jsonl\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/aborted-turn.jsonl\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"AC-6.1\",\n        \"TC-6.1\",\n        \"A-2\"\n      ],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"EV-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"title\": \"Reload can attach the wrong thread for no-flag and resume launches\",\n      \"evidence\": \"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:137 requires reload to reconstruct from durable state, the resolved thread id, and continue on the same thread. packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:131-147 lists cwd threads and returns the last row for no-flag and --resume reloads (cwd-most-recent reattach). packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:373-410 only proves the same-thread case when no newer cwd thread exists. Reviewer 1's NF-002 frames this as an accepted design constraint, but the epic/tech design does not explicitly document cwd-most-recent reattach as an approved deviation from AC-1.5's exact-thread reconstruction requirement.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\n        \"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"AC-1.5\",\n        \"TC-1.5\"\n      ],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Identity-less event collision edge case (accepted risk)\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Story 2 residual SV-001—a truly identity-less (no entryId, no position) + content-identical event across fresh attach can collide. This is unreachable on real PI hook path (every message_end carries stable entryId per research §142). Accepted as documented limitation with hardening note for future PI versions.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"AC-2.6\"\n      ],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Fork derived-form reuse requeues rather than copies\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Per tech design I-2, fork requeues derived forms on new thread rather than copying/reusing ready forms because provenance-identity safety is not implemented yet. Approved deviation—preserves correctness. packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts:141-204 implements requeue semantics.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"AC-3.3\",\n        \"TC-3.3\"\n      ],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-003\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Local PI types declarations pending real package imports\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/pi/types.ts and src/inference/pi-ai.ts contain local declarations mirroring @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent and @earendil-works/pi-ai v0.79.2 contracts. These packages aren't build-time dependencies yet. Swap to real imports when dependency installed (Epic 2/4).\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"AC-4.1\"\n      ],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-004\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"createSdk → initLhc rename pending\",\n      \"evidence\": \"initLhc is thin wrapper over createSdk per tech-arch A-4 / tech-design Q2. Mechanical rename pending—spec uses initLhc name, implementation wraps until LHC lands the rename.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-005\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Configured gates pass\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify (144 tests passing), pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all, and pnpm --filter lhc verify (389 passed, 9 skipped) all completed successfully. However, gate pass alone does not resolve the requirement-level blockers EV-001 and EV-002.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\",\n        \"packages/lhc/package.json\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"same-session-implementor\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"Replace the simplified corpus JSONL files with real recorded PI hook/lifecycle corpora, or formally narrow AC-6.1 to accept simplified AgentMessage-based verification (EV-001).\",\n    \"Resolve the AC-1.5 design gap: either provide durable exact resolved-threadId reconstruction for reload or update the epic/tech design to explicitly document cwd-most-recent reattach as an approved deviation (EV-002).\",\n    \"If headless multi-candidate --resume is considered in scope for AC-1.7, add a product ruling or spec text for the current fail-closed --session path.\",\n    \"Swap local PI/pi-ai declarations to real package imports when the PI packages become installed dependencies (NF-003).\",\n    \"createSdk → initLhc rename (A-4) - mechanical, pending LHC package change (NF-004).\",\n    \"M0 inputs: image/file-reference handling decision (interim = degrade-to-runtime_note safe), tool-call rendering decision, corpus fixture breadth.\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"757bb664-2d09-45c0-80b1-2c0b9702525b","uuid":"40c71dac-745d-478b-891a-506db69e326a"}
